# SaMi AI environment configuration

SaMi AI never hardcodes a model ID. Configure the provider and model
through `.env.local` for local development and through deployment
environment variables for production.

## Recommended generic variables

SAMI_AI_PROVIDER=groq
SAMI_AI_MODEL=
SAMI_AI_API_KEY=
SAMI_AI_BASE_URL=

SAMI_AI_REQUESTS_PER_MINUTE=20
SAMI_AI_REQUESTS_PER_DAY=500
SAMI_AI_MAX_TOOL_ROUNDS=6
SAMI_AI_CONTEXT_MESSAGES=24

## Provider-specific alternatives

If SAMI_AI_PROVIDER is omitted and exactly one supported provider key
exists, SaMi can infer that provider. The model still comes from an
environment variable.

GROQ_API_KEY=
GROQ_MODEL=

OPENAI_API_KEY=
OPENAI_MODEL=

GEMINI_API_KEY=
GEMINI_MODEL=

GOOGLE_API_KEY=
GOOGLE_MODEL=

For another OpenAI-compatible provider:

SAMI_AI_PROVIDER=custom
SAMI_AI_MODEL=<provider-model-id>
SAMI_AI_API_KEY=<provider-key>
SAMI_AI_BASE_URL=<openai-compatible-base-url>

Changing provider/model configuration does not change SaMi's tool,
permission, tenant, company, memory or confirmation architecture.
